# HTML/CSS Profile Website

A simple personal profile website created with HTML and CSS.

## Getting Started

These instructions explain how to open and view the website on your local machine.

### Prerequisites

You need:
- A web browser (e.g. Chrome)
- A code editor (e.g. Visual Studio Code or IntelliJ IDEA)

### Installation

1. Clone or download the repository.
2. Open the `frontend/html-basics` folder.
3. Open `index.html` in your web browser.

No additional installation is required.

## Usage

The website contains:
- A personal introduction
- Information about my apprenticeship
- An overview of the IT skills I have learned

The website uses CSS for styling and responsive design.

## Technologies

- HTML5
- CSS3

## Project Structure

- frontend/html_basics/ – HTML exercises

- frontend/css_basics/ – CSS stylesheets

- frontend/img/ – Images used in the website